{title: Steadfast Love}
{subtitle: Psalms 85:9}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] | [Dm] [C] |
| [Bb] | [Dm] [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Will you be [Dm]angry [C]with us for[Bb]ever
Prolong your [Dm]anger [C]through all genera[Bb]tions
Will you [Dm]not revive [C]us a[Dm]gain
So your peo[Bb]ple may re[C]joice in [Dm]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Stead[C]fast love [Bb]and faithfulness have [Dm]met
Right[C]eousness [Bb]and peace have kissed
[Dm]Faithful[C]ness springs [Bb]up from the earth
[Gm]Righteousness looks [Am]down from [Dm]heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Show us your [C]steadfast love [Bb]Lord
[Dm]Grant us your [C]salvation [Bb]now
Let me [Dm]hear what God [C]the Lord will [Bb]speak
He will [Gm]speak [Am7]peace to his [Dm]people
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Steadfast [C]love and [Bb]faithfulness have met
[Dm]Right[C]eousness [Bb]and peace have kissed
[Dm]Faithful[C]ness springs [Bb]up from the earth
[Gm]Righteousness looks [Am]down from [Dm]heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
To his [Bb]faithful ones [C]let them not turn [Dm]back
[Bb]They must not [C]turn back to [Dm]folly
[Bb]Surely his sal[C]vation is [Dm]near to those
Who [Bb]fear him and [C]dwell in his [Dm]land
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Steadfast [C]love and [Bb]faithfulness have met
[Dm]Righteous[C]ness and [Bb]peace have kissed
[Dm]Faithful[C]ness springs [Bb]up from the earth
[Gm]Righteousness looks [Am]down from [Dm]heaven
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
That glory may dwell in our [C]land
[Bb]Peace to [C]his peo[Dm][C][Bb]ple [Dm][C][Dm]
{end_of_verse}
